I've got something half-functional running under Linux.  It took some
tweaking, mainly to get it to create files in the playground without
running into trouble with the Unix security model.  Also it seems to have
a bug in the monster spawning that causes it to print a null character;
the display code is set to panic when it sees this, and for better
diagnosis I've tweaked it to substitute a non-ASCII character.  The result
seems to be a monster with a null string for a name.

The save-file code does not seem to work correctly, and there seem to be
problems when moving to a new level.

Overall it looks rather like Hack 1.0 without distinct roles; you start
off with armor, a sword, some food, and a dog.  The lighting model seems
to be that of Hack and of NetHack through 3.0.10:  a room is either all
lit, or all unlit.  Some commands that we now take for granted are not
there.  Monsters don't seem to leave corpses; how that will affect food
management is not clear at this time.

